  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The development hereby approved shall not be commenced prior to the submission and approval of a Fire Safety Strategy pursuant to Policy 12 (A) of the London Plan.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "The rating level of noise emitted from the extraction plant hereby permitted shall be at least 5 dBA lower than the existing background noise level at any time during operation. The noise level shall be measured or predicted 1.0 m externally from the window of any habitable room of the nearest residential property, in accordance with British Standard BS 4142:2014.\r\rReason: To protect the amenity of nearby residential occupiers from noise and disturbance, to comply with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to the first operation of the Class E(b) use hereby approved, the kitchen extraction system shall be fully installed and commissioned strictly in accordance with Section 5.5 of the approved Noise Report, including:  \r\ra) The extraction fan unit must be installed internally within the building structure.  \r\rb) An Acoustica R02-5-2100 (or an equivalent alternative matching or exceeding its stated octave-band insertion loss profile) discharge silencer fitted on the discharge side of the fan system.  \r\rc) The entire ducted network and fan unit structurally isolated from the building frame using high-resilience rubber/neoprene anti-vibration pedestal mountings and flexible duct connectors to prevent structure-borne noise and vibration transmission. \r\rReason: To ensure adequate noise attenuation and vibration isolation in order to safeguard neighbour amenity, to comply with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The extraction flue and ventilation equipment hereby approved shall be maintained and cleaned strictly in accordance with the maintenance schedule set out in the approved Extraction Report for the lifetime of the development.  \r\rReason: To ensure effective odour control and mitigate potential impacts on residential amenity from cooking fumes, to comply with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
